Solution Overview:
General presentation of the solution
1. Detailed description of how it works
The solution consists of a structured training and support program aimed at equipping disadvantaged young people in Chad with digital skills that can be directly applied in the job market and in digital entrepreneurship.
The process includes:
- Identification and selection of beneficiaries through a participatory community assessment;
- Progressive training in three levels.

a. Basic digital skills (office automation, online communication, information search).
b. Intermediate skills (website creation, e-commerce, digital marketing).
c. Advanced skills (introduction to coding, data analysis, basic cybersecurity).

- Practical projects enabling learners to create real products or services for local stakeholders.
- Post-training support: mentoring, networking with employers, or micro-business incubation.

2. Methodologies and technologies used

A. Methodologies:

- Design Thinking to co-create content based on local needs;
- Competency-Based Learning approach ensuring practical mastery of acquired knowledge;
- Experiential learning (Learning by Doing) through interactive workshops and real-life cases;
- Blended learning combining face-to-face classes and online modules.

B. Technologies:
- Open source LMS platforms (Moodle) for course management;
- Collaborative and cloud tools (Google Workspace, Trello, Slack);
- Graphic design software (Canva, GIMP) and web development software (WordPress, HTML/CSS, JavaScript);
- Digital monitoring and evaluation systems to measure progress and impact (KoboToolbox, Google Forms).

3. Partnerships and collaboration models

- Local NGOs and community associations: mobilization and monitoring of beneficiaries;
- Technology companies and startups: mentoring, internships, professional integration;
- Academic institutions: certification and official recognition of skills;
- Technical partners and donors: provision of equipment, financial support, and capacity building.
This model is based on shared governance and mutual commitments to ensure sustainability and local ownership.

Desired impact:
Objectives of the solution:
- Reduce the digital divide among disadvantaged young people in Chad by providing them with access to practical training in digital skills;
- Promote professional integration and digital entrepreneurship to help reduce youth unemployment;
- Stimulate local innovation by strengthening the technical capacities of beneficiaries;
- Promote social and economic inclusion through access to digital technologies.

Key achievements and impacts (quantifiable):
- More than 20 young people trained since January 2024, 30% of whom have found employment or started a digital-related micro-business;
- Estimated 25% reduction in unemployment among beneficiaries thanks to the acquisition of digital skills;
- Creation of five local digital startups incubated with post-training support;
- Implementation of a digitalized monitoring and evaluation system resulting in an 85% certification success rate;
- Indirect contribution to improving access to information and online services in the areas covered, impacting approximately 2,000 people in local communities.

Key technologies:
Key technologies used in the solution:

- Open source LMS platforms (Moodle): for managing, delivering, and monitoring online training modules;
- Cloud-based collaboration tools (Google Workspace, Trello, Slack): for communication, project management, and remote teamwork;
- Free graphic design and web development software (Canva, GIMP, WordPress, HTML/CSS, JavaScript): for developing practical skills in design, web development, and digital marketing;
- Digital monitoring and evaluation systems (KoboToolbox, Google Forms): for collecting and analyzing data and measuring impact in real time.
- Mobile technologies: use of smartphone-compatible applications and platforms to maximize access for young people, even in areas with poor infrastructure.

Currently, the solution does not yet integrate artificial intelligence (AI), IoT, or blockchain, but it remains open to the future integration of these technologies to improve the personalization of training and the traceability of certifications.

Unique Characteristics:
Unique and innovative features of the solution:
- Hybrid and adaptive training model combining face-to-face and online learning (blended learning), allowing for great flexibility and accessibility, particularly in low-connectivity contexts;
- Learner-centered approach based on Design Thinking and competency-based pedagogy, ensuring that content is tailored to the real needs of young people and the local market.
- Strong multisectoral partnerships involving local NGOs, tech startups, public institutions, and donors, promoting shared governance and better professional integration of beneficiaries;
- Use of open source tools and free software that guarantee sustainability and cost reduction, while promoting the development of learners' technical skills;
- Innovative digital monitoring and evaluation mechanisms with precise indicators enabling rapid program adjustment and transparency in reporting;
- A mixed financing model integrating local resources, international partnerships, and in-kind contributions, ensuring the program's sustainability and gradual expansion.

