Solution Overview:
How it Works

DÉSINFOX Connect is a digital initiative that trains young people, particularly those from vulnerable backgrounds, to recognize, analyze, and counter online disinformation. It combines in-person and online training, interactive social media campaigns, the creation of content verified by young people themselves (participatory fact-checking), and ongoing support via collaborative digital platforms.
Methodologies and Technologies Used
The solution is based on an active and inclusive pedagogy based on media and information literacy (MIL), the development of critical digital skills, and project-based learning. It uses:
• open-source content analysis and fact-checking tools (InVID, Google Fact Check Tools, etc.);
• a mobile/web platform for self-training and interactive quizzes;
• collective intelligence via moderated discussion groups and webinars.

Partnerships and Collaboration Models
DÉSINFOX Connect is implemented in collaboration with local associations, universities, journalists, youth organizations, and public institutions. The project is based on a tripartite partnership model:
1. Community, for strong local roots;
2. Institutional, with ministries (education, youth, communication) for sustainability;
3. Technical, with experts and stakeholders in MIL and cybersecurity.
This multi-stakeholder approach promotes adaptable scaling and local ownership of skills, while strengthening the information resilience of young people.
